From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:42:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/26] plan9: std's fs, env, paths, pipes, processes, network;
 os::fd, os::plan9

Files on open/create and stat(5) entries (rename stays in a directory, across
them a file is copied); /env; processes forked off the shared stacks onto the
child's own segment, waited for through /proc/n/wait from any thread; the
network of /net (dial, announce, listen, accept; UDP with headers; names
through /net/cs); close-on-exec for pipes and network descriptors through #d.
What a descriptor has beyond the kernel's (append mode, timeouts, UDP peer) is
kept beside it: std views a File or TcpStream as only its descriptor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
